// An acciaccatura of two (or more) notes is drawn with no slash: the beamed pair in bar 1 comes
// out the same as the plain grace group in bar 2. LilyPond draws the acciaccatura's slash through
// the beam (the stroke that a lone acciaccatura gets through its flag). Found by the OMR's grace
// note work (S21, 2026-10-18): the reading cannot tell the two apart on the page, and the
// generator writes no beamed acciaccatura until the slash is drawn.
// (lysc png this file: bar 1's pair and bar 2's pair look alike; a lone acciaccatura in bar 3 has its slash)
// (2026-10-20: written again in the current score syntax, with octave absolute; the drawing is the same)
octave absolute
time 4/4
key c major

part p1 { clef treble }

section Piece {
  p1 {
    acciaccatura { e'16 f'16 } g'4 a'4 b'4 c''4 |
    grace { e'16 f'16 } g'4 a'4 b'4 c''4 |
    acciaccatura { f'8 } g'4 a'4 b'4 c''4 |
  }
}

form { ~Piece }

score {
  staff p1 "Staff"
}
